        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Resolve bfcid slot in sponsored credential key links",
        "summary": "Added `trackedSponsoredCredentials` to fill the `{bfcid}` slot in declared credential key-page URLs with the run's signed click id, mirroring Desktop and Cloud behavior. If no signed id is available, the link is dropped rather than shown with a literal placeholder, and the `{email}` slot is removed to prevent unauthorized email sharing. `SponsoredRun.startTurn` now passes runtime inputs to this resolver, and `SponsoredAccountPrompt` accepts an injectable `openUrl` handler so the resolved link is opened in the user's browser when clicked.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "New export `trackedSponsoredCredentials` in `cli/src/utils/sponsored-account-step.ts` maps declared credentials through `resolveSponsoredBfcidTemplate` and `signupUrlWithEmail`; `cli/src/utils/sponsored-run.ts` now calls this function instead of passing raw `declaredRunCredentials` to the account step; `SponsoredAccountPrompt` accepts an injectable `openUrl` prop to render resolved key-page links.",
