        "calls": 1,
        "text": "When a sponsored task in the terminal assistant asks you to provide a login link, that link now includes a unique tracking code that identifies your specific session, ensuring the advertiser knows you came from this particular offer. If a tracking code is not available, the link is simply not shown rather than displaying a broken placeholder, and any field that would have sent your email address to the advertiser has been removed to protect your privacy. This affects developers using the free tier who run sponsored tasks in the terminal, and the visible result is a cleaner sign-in prompt that links directly to your session without sharing unnecessary personal details.",
