        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Guard sponsored account links against unfilled click ids",
        "summary": "This commit centralizes sponsored link resolution in the new `common/src/ads/sponsored-run-links.ts` module, replacing per-call-site logic with a single resolver that fills the signed click id into sign-up and credential key pages. The CLI's account prompt now applies a last-resort guard (`shownSponsoredLink`) that prevents any link containing a literal `{bfcid}` placeholder from being drawn or opened. When a link is blocked, the guard falls back to the Accept's signed advertiser link if available, or omits the link entirely, and emits the `UNFILLED_CLICK_ID_BLOCKED_METRIC` warning. This ensures sign-ups are always attributed and never routed to a placeholder URL, fixing a gap where the CLI key form could previously open an unattributed link.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The new file `common/src/ads/sponsored-run-links.ts` introduces `resolveSponsoredRunLinks` and `guardSponsoredLink` to centralize link resolution. In `cli/src/components/sponsored-account-prompt.tsx`, the `TerminalLink` components for sign-in and credentials are now wrapped by a new `shownSponsoredLink` guard that blocks URLs matching the `UNFILLED_CLICK_ID` regex.",
